Framebuffer driver for the display of the Google Pixel 7

The driver 'exynos_fb' is a port of the vendor's Linux display driver
(exynos-drm) and panel driver. It takes over the display pipeline as set up
by the boot loader. It needs the ports 'pixel_linux', 'google_display', and
'google_soc_gs'.

The scenario 'run/exynos_fb_pixel' shows a test pattern on the display:

! make run/exynos_fb_pixel KERNEL=hw BOARD=google_pixel7
